      "hints": [
        "Differentiate $V = \\frac{4}{3}\\pi r^3$ to get $\\frac{dV}{dr} = 4\\pi r^2$.",
        "Use $\\frac{dr}{dt} = \\frac{dV/dt}{dV/dr} = \\frac{50}{4\\pi r^2}$ at $r = 10\\text{ cm}$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Differentiate the spherical volume formula with respect to radius $r$:\n$$\\frac{dV}{dr} = 4\\pi r^2$$",
        "Apply the chain rule for connected rates of change:\n$$\\frac{dr}{dt} = \\frac{\\frac{dV}{dt}}{\\frac{dV}{dr}} = \\frac{50}{4\\pi r^2}$$",
        "Evaluate at $r = 10\\text{ cm}$:\n$$\\frac{dr}{dt} = \\frac{50}{4\\pi(10^2)} = \\frac{50}{400\\pi} = \\frac{1}{8\\pi} \\approx 0.0398\\text{ cm s}^{-1} \\quad (\\text{to 3 s.f.})$$"
      ],
